@startuml
title FindBar lifecycle (per Tab)

[*] --> Closed

state Closed {
}

state FindOnly {
}

state FindReplace {
}

Closed --> FindOnly : ⌘F\n(open(false, ...))
Closed --> FindReplace : ⌘R\n(open(true, ...))
FindOnly --> FindReplace : ⌘R\n(replace row revealed,\nquery/matches kept)
FindReplace --> FindReplace : ⌘F\n(no-op: already open)

FindOnly --> Closed : Escape / close button
FindReplace --> Closed : Escape / close button

FindOnly --> FindOnly : query/option edit\n(refresh, §3.2)
FindReplace --> FindReplace : query/option edit,\nReplace, Replace All\n(refresh, §3.2/§3.8)

note right of Closed
  query / replacement / options / scope
  are preserved across Closed <-> open
  transitions on the SAME tab (§3.7).
  Switching tabs shows a DIFFERENT
  Tab's own FindBar, starting from
  its own last state.
end note

@enduml
